    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: net/sched: ets: Always remove class from active list before deleting in ets_qdisc_change (CVE-2025-71066)\n\n* kernel: procfs: fix missing RCU protection when reading real_parent in do_task_stat() (CVE-2026-46259)\n\n* kernel: nvmet-tcp: check INIT_FAILED before nvmet_req_uninit in digest error path (CVE-2026-64534)\n\n* kernel: Linux kernel: libceph stack out-of-bounds write via crafted OSDMap (CVE-2026-68159)\n\n* kernel: libceph: refresh auth-\u003eauthorizer_buf{,_len} after authorizer update (CVE-2026-68156)\n\n* kernel: Linux kernel (libceph): Denial of Service due to malformed monitor maps (CVE-2026-68155)\n\n* kernel: ipvs: reload ip header after head reallocation (CVE-2026-68476)\n\n* kernel: ipvs: clear IPv4 options after rebasing tunnel ICMP errors (CVE-2026-74669)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: usx2y: bound the hwdep mmap fault offset (CVE-2026-74641)\n\n* kernel: ipvs: do not propagate one-packet flag to synced conns (CVE-2026-80714)\n\n* kernel: nvme-tcp: fix host memory disclosure on R2T for a read command (CVE-2026-89481)\n\n* kernel: ipv4: free inet_opt and ireq_opt after an RCU grace period (CVE-2026-98432)\n\n* kernel: ZDI-CAN-33367: Linux Kernel skbuff skb_zerocopy Improper Ownership Management Local Privilege Escalation Vulnerability ()\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Critical Bug Fixes for customer issues with lpfc [rhel-8.6.z] (JIRA:RHEL-286150)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
